description:
**Publication date:**  

23/06/2026



**Job type:**  

Full\-time



**Salary:**  

Up to $3'000 / month



Technologies



n8n



Make.com



Python



LLM APIs



PostgreSQL



REST APIs



We're hiring a Senior AI Engineer to design and ship

automation that connects our tools, data and AI models. You'll build reliable

workflows in n8n and Make.com, back them with Python services and databases, and

wire in large language models to automate real business processes end\-to\-end —

from data ingestion to action. This is a hands\-on, high\-ownership role: you'll

turn fuzzy business needs into dependable automated systems and own the platform

they run on.



What you'll do



Design, build and maintain automation workflows in n8n and Make.com;

Integrate third\-party APIs, webhooks and internal services into reliable end\-to\-end pipelines;

Write Python services, glue code and scheduled jobs that extend what no\-code tools can do on their own;

Model, store and query data in SQL databases that back the automations;

Integrate LLM / AI APIs — prompt design, retrieval\-augmented generation (RAG) and structured extraction — to automate real business tasks;

Add monitoring, error handling, retries and alerting so workflows run dependably in production;

Document the platform and own it as it grows.



Requirements



3\+ years building automations and integrations, with hands\-on experience in n8n and/or Make.com (Zapier a plus);

Solid Python for scripting, API integration and data transformation;

Strong SQL and relational\-database skills (PostgreSQL preferred) — querying, joins and schema design;

Comfortable with REST APIs, webhooks, JSON and OAuth / authentication flows;

Practical experience integrating LLM / AI APIs (OpenAI or similar) into real workflows;

Understanding of error handling, idempotency, rate limits and observability in automations;

**Bonus:** Docker, vector databases / RAG, message queues, and JavaScript for n8n Function nodes;

Clear English and the ability to turn fuzzy business needs into reliable automated processes.



We provide our engineers



Free English classes, technical lectures and courses.



You get 22 working days of annual leave.



We pay for your illness. We don't need a sick list.



An ability to plan your working day.



Modern cozy office in the city center.

We are looking for a skilled and motivated AI Engineer to join our forward\-thinking team. The ideal candidate is passionate about building cutting\-edge AI solutions, has a strong technical foundation, and excels in collaborative environments. As an AI Engineer, you will play a key role in designing, developing, and maintaining advanced data products and AI\-powered applications. You’ll work closely with cross\-functional teams—including Data Scientists, Analytics Engineers, Front\-End Developers, and ML Engineers—to deliver scalable and impactful solutions.





Now, if you were to come on board as our AI Engineer, we’d ask you to do the following:


* Develop and maintain scalable AI applications from concept to deployment;


* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features;


* Architect and implement efficient and reusable AI systems;


* Write clean, well\-documented, and maintainable code following best practices;


* Conduct code reviews, provide constructive feedback and mentor junior team members;


* Staying up\-to\-date with emerging AI technologies and industry trends to drive continuous improvement.





Think you have what it takes to be our AI Engineer? Here’s how we’ll know:


* Bachelor's degree in a STEM field (or equivalent experience);


* Strong experience with Large Language Models (LLMs), RAG, embeddings;


* 2\+ years of experience developing AI / data products in a hands\-on capacity;


* Proficiency in the modern data science stack (Python, NumPy, pandas);


* Strong cloud engineering skills and ample experience taking AI ideas to production;


* Experience with database systems (SQL and NoSQL) and data warehouses;


* Familiarity with RESTful APIs;


* Knowledge of version control systems (e.g., Git) and agile development methodologies;


* Excellent problem\-solving skills, attention to detail, and ability to work independently or in a team environment;


* Excellent written and verbal communication skills with experience in relaying complex concepts to non\-technical users.




* Position Title: AI Engineer
* Salary: 110,000\.00 \- 150,000\.00
* Employment Type: Full Time, Permanent
* Hybrid: 3 Days a Week \- Toronto/ Mississauga




*In accordance with provincial legislation and our commitment to transparent hiring practices, the compensation range for this position is provided. Final compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, and internal equity. Canadian work experience is not required. Please note that artificial intelligence tools are utilized in the applicant screening process.*

